WEBVTT

c0
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.649
This is a story about
what to do on a date.

c1
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.000
It begins one early summer afternoon.

c2
00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:15.340
It begins with Jeff.

c3
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.090
And Kay. And Nick.

c4
00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:31.030
Of course, you may not have a
problem about what to do on a date,

c5
00:00:31.149 --> 00:00:34.750
but Nick, well, he has
a real dating problem.

c6
00:00:35.639 --> 00:00:38.560
If he took Kay out on a
date, what would they do?

c7
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.759
Where would they go?

c8
00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:47.316
Just a minute, Jeff. I'll get my tennis

c9
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.299
racket. OK, Nick, but hurry.

c10
00:01:05.474 --> 00:01:07.975
Hey, what about asking Kay
to come to the community

c11
00:01:08.059 --> 00:01:11.139
center with us on Friday to
fix up that scavenger sale?

c12
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.769
We could make it a double date. What?

c13
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.800
You heard what I said.

c14
00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.040
That's no place to take a girl on a date,

c15
00:01:22.519 --> 00:01:26.110
helping to fix up the
scavenger sale, is it?

c16
00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.099
Why not? On a first date

c17
00:01:29.849 --> 00:01:30.850
First date.

c18
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.239
Yeah. Well, Kay's a swell girl.

c19
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.339
I was gonna, I was
thinking of calling her,

c20
00:01:38.819 --> 00:01:40.510
maybe ask her to the show Friday.

c21
00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.580
Good picture, wagon train.

c22
00:01:42.755 --> 00:01:46.856
Well, hurry up and call her and let's get
going. I still have to get my things yet.

c23
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.019
Call her now?

c24
00:01:48.339 --> 00:01:50.779
Sure. You know the number, don't you?

c25
00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:53.890
OK.

c26
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.220
What if she says no.

c27
00:02:10.188 --> 00:02:11.578
Oh, hello, Kay.

c28
00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.238
This is Nick Baxter.

c29
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:16.979
Oh, hello, Nick. How are you?

c30
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:18.721
Fine, thanks.

c31
00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:23.779
Say, Kay, next Friday, would you like
to see Wagon Train at the movies?

c32
00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.250
Oh, I'm sorry, Nick.

c33
00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.160
I suppose you've got your
mind made up to see it.

c34
00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:32.595
You've seen it. She's already seen

c35
00:02:32.679 --> 00:02:34.780
it. Well, ask her about the scavenger sal.

c36
00:02:36.039 --> 00:02:37.040
Go ahead.

c37
00:02:37.869 --> 00:02:41.386
Uh, Kay, you wouldn't want
to help get the scavenger

c38
00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.320
sale ready at the community
center, would you?

c39
00:02:45.479 --> 00:02:47.550
Oh, I've been hearing about that.

c40
00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.589
Yes, I'd like to very much.

c41
00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:55.080
You would. All right,
I'll call for you then,

c42
00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:56.860
about 7. Bye.

c43
00:02:59.889 --> 00:03:03.009
I sure didn't think she'd go to
a place like that for a date.

c44
00:03:05.539 --> 00:03:09.380
Where's my racket? Oh, ready?

c45
00:03:09.464 --> 00:03:12.865
You know, you'd better think some
more, fellow, about what to do on a

c46
00:03:12.949 --> 00:03:15.470
date. Do you think
she'll have a good time?

c47
00:03:16.169 --> 00:03:19.220
What do you suppose I'll have
to do? Do you know who's gonna?

c48
00:03:32.509 --> 00:03:33.510
Now,

c49
00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:38.360
you may not have thought of this sort
of thing as a place to take a date,

c50
00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.521
but it looks like it could be fun.

c51
00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.089
A group doing things together.

c52
00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.610
Pretty good idea for a first date.

c53
00:03:57.419 --> 00:04:00.369
Plenty to do, plenty of people to talk to.

c54
00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.619
But let's see if Nick
and Kay are enjoying it.

c55
00:04:06.419 --> 00:04:09.505
No amount of stuff could make
this thing look any older. Boy,

c56
00:04:09.589 --> 00:04:11.050
that is an old-timer.

c57
00:04:24.545 --> 00:04:25.546
Can you help

c58
00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.640
me put this sign up?

c59
00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.800
Oh, sure.

c60
00:04:31.549 --> 00:04:33.170
I can't quite reach that far.

c61
00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:37.456
How's this? That's about

c62
00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.541
right.

c63
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.951
say, Kay,

c64
00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:49.929
-are you really having a
good time? -Of course I am.

c65
00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.920
I'm glad you thought of
coming here. So am I.

c66
00:04:54.589 --> 00:04:55.590
Uh, I mean,

c67
00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.279
Yes, it was a good idea.

c68
00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.630
OK, how about helping with
refreshments for the game?

c69
00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.470
All right, see you later.

c70
00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:08.519
-Oh, yeah, -sure.

c71
00:05:11.059 --> 00:05:12.281
Got any more tacks?

c72
00:05:12.365 --> 00:05:14.016
I think they're over there by the

c73
00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.101
door.

c74
00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.799
Yes, it was a good idea to come here.

c75
00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.690
How does Jeff get ideas like that?

c76
00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.619
Hey, what's this?

c77
00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.079
Maybe this is where Jeff gets ideas.

c78
00:05:32.209 --> 00:05:33.929
A list of coming activities.

c79
00:05:35.279 --> 00:05:36.470
A bike trip.

c80
00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.201
That could be a lot of fun.

c81
00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.130
A chance to do things with
a group, to get acquainted.

c82
00:05:42.829 --> 00:05:46.630
It does look like a good time
if your partner likes it.

c83
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.100
Would Kay enjoy a bike trip?

c84
00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.579
Or a weenie roast.

c85
00:05:55.859 --> 00:05:59.176
Another group date, a chance to learn the

c86
00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.959
give and take of working
and playing together.

c87
00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.940
Not much arranging
needed, not much expense,

c88
00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.600
and that can be important.

c89
00:06:07.179 --> 00:06:10.100
Could be a fine date if Kay would like it.

c90
00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.841
Wonder if she'd like to
go to a baseball game.

c91
00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.500
A date that's not too involved, one
you can carry through comfortably.

c92
00:06:18.549 --> 00:06:21.179
And there are all sorts
of other sports events,

c93
00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.109
inexpensive dates, most of them.

c94
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.901
Swimming meets, for example.

c95
00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:32.209
You can find many good ideas for dates.

c96
00:06:34.299 --> 00:06:36.899
Dates that give you a good
chance to get acquainted.

c97
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.649
And dates that you don't have to
worry too much about in advance.

c98
00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:48.709
It was a good deal coming here tonight,
double dating with Jeff and Phyllis.

c99
00:06:51.149 --> 00:06:54.709
When all 4 are good friends
and enjoy the same things,

c100
00:06:54.829 --> 00:06:56.470
double dates can be lots of fun.

c101
00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.190
Or you can ask Kate to go
on dates with you alone,

c102
00:07:00.769 --> 00:07:04.486
if you plan for what she enjoys. Hey,

c103
00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.005
you loafer. What are you doing

c104
